  "label": "User projected onto the accusatory pointing gesture of Donald Trump",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of Donald Trump pointing outward with an accusatory gesture. This projection is implicit, as the meme uses the gesture and the text to imply that the viewer (user) is being addressed or is expected to align with the policy being promoted. The pointing gesture directs blame or responsibility, and the user is implicitly positioned as the one who should understand or accept the policy's justification. The text 'would've stopped that' further reinforces this by suggesting the user is being asked to consider the policy's purported effectiveness, thereby projecting the user onto the scene of judgment or decision-making.",
